@using Booster.Licensing.Portal.Services
<div class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
        <p class="kicker reveal">Download</p>
        <div class="page-head-grid" style="margin-top:0;align-items:start">
            <div>
                <h1 class="reveal d2">Three commands to <em>your own server</em>.</h1>
                <p class="lede reveal d3" style="margin-top:28px">The Docker Compose package: every service, PostgreSQL, Redis, Kafka, OpenFGA and the admin console in one
                    folder. The setup script generates every password and key on your server, so there are no secrets to fill in by hand.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="dl-card reveal d3">
                <div class="file"><b>@InstallPackage.FileName</b><span>about 15 KB</span></div>
                <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/download/@InstallPackage.FileName" data-download>Download the package <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
                <ul class="facts">
                    <li>Free to download; you get the license after installing.</li>
                    <li>Runs with Docker on Linux, macOS and Windows.</li>
                    <li>Internet access is only needed to pull images.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<section class="install" aria-labelledby="h-steps" style="margin-top:80px">
    <div class="wrap inst-grid">
        <div class="reveal">
            <p class="kicker">Installation</p>
            <h2 id="h-steps">From download to first sign-in.</h2>
            <ol class="steps" style="margin-top:32px">
                <li><span class="n">Step 1</span><div><h3>Unpack</h3><p>Unzip the file and change into the <code>booster-auth</code> folder.</p></div></li>
                <li><span class="n">Step 2</span><div><h3>Run the script</h3><p>It asks for your Booster Auth address (e.g. <code>auth.company.com</code>), the HTTPS port, the console
                    port and the admin e-mail, then generates every password and key at random and writes <code>.env</code>. Its prompts are in Turkish.</p></div></li>
                <li><span class="n">Step 3</span><div><h3>Start</h3><p><code>docker compose up -d</code>. The first start pulls the images and creates the databases and the HTTPS certificate.</p></div></li>
                <li><span class="n">Step 4</span><div><h3>Open the console</h3><p>Sign in at <code>http://localhost:3000</code> as <code>admin</code>; you set a new password on first sign-in.</p></div></li>
            </ol>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal d2">
            <div class="term" role="region" aria-label="Linux and macOS installation commands">
                <div class="term-bar"><span>Linux / macOS</span><span>bash</span></div>
<pre><code><span class="p">$ </span>unzip booster-auth.zip &amp;&amp; cd booster-auth
<span class="p">$ </span>./kurulum.sh
<span class="ok">.env olusturuldu.</span>
<span class="p">$ </span>docker compose up -d</code></pre>
            </div>
            <div class="term" role="region" aria-label="Windows installation commands">
                <div class="term-bar"><span>Windows</span><span>PowerShell</span></div>
<pre><code><span class="p">&gt; </span>Expand-Archive booster-auth.zip .
<span class="p">&gt; </span>cd booster-auth
<span class="p">&gt; </span>powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\kurulum.ps1
<span class="p">&gt; </span>docker compose up -d</code></pre>
            </div>
            <p class="hard">If a secret is still <code>CHANGE_ME</code>, the system refuses to start and names the missing variable. An installation cannot
                start on placeholder values.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="h-prompts">
    <div class="wrap split">
        <div class="reveal">
            <p class="kicker">Setup script</p>
            <h2 id="h-prompts">Four questions, the rest is automatic.</h2>
            <p class="prose-2" style="margin-top:20px">These are the values the script asks for. Database, Redis and OpenFGA passwords, the password pepper, the encryption
                key and the console session secret are never asked; they are all generated at random.</p>
            <div class="callout tip" style="margin-top:24px"><p><b>Local trial.</b> If your address is not in DNS yet, add <code>127.0.0.1 auth.company.com</code>
                to your <code>hosts</code> file. The Booster Auth address must be on one of the domains in your license.</p></div>
        </div>
        <table class="qa reveal d2">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Prompt</th><th scope="col">Example</th><th scope="col">Meaning</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><th scope="row">Booster Auth address</th><td><code>auth.company.com</code></td><td>Where your applications send users to sign in; the OIDC issuer is built from it.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">HTTPS port</th><td><code>443</code></td><td>Use e.g. <code>8443</code> if 443 is taken.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Console port / address</th><td><code>3000</code></td><td>Where the admin console runs, e.g. <code>http://localhost:3000</code>.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Admin e-mail</th><td><code>it@@company.com</code></td><td>The first administrator's e-mail. The username is always <code>admin</code>.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="band" aria-labelledby="h-req">
    <div class="wrap split">
        <div class="reveal">
            <p class="kicker">Requirements</p>
            <h2 id="h-req" style="margin-bottom:32px">A single machine is enough.</h2>
            <ul class="req">
                <li><b>Docker</b><span>Docker Engine 24+ and Docker Compose v2 (Windows / macOS: Docker Desktop)</span></li>
                <li><b>Memory</b><span>At least 4 GB free</span></li>
                <li><b>Disk</b><span>10 GB</span></li>
                <li><b>Network</b><span>Images are pulled from <code>ghcr.io/booster-tr</code> during installation</span></li>
                <li><b>Included</b><span>PostgreSQL, Redis, Kafka and OpenFGA; nothing else to install</span></li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal d2">
            <p class="kicker">Package contents</p>
            <h2 style="margin-bottom:32px;font-size:clamp(26px,2.6vw,32px)">Plain, readable files.</h2>
            <ul class="files">
                @foreach (var f in Model.PackageFiles)
                {
                    <li>booster-auth/@f</li>
                }
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<div class="closing">
    <div class="wrap closing-inner">
        <h2 class="reveal">The details are in the documentation.</h2>
        <div class="side-cta reveal d2">
            <p>.env variables, the HTTPS certificate, first sign-in and license activation, step by step.</p>
            <div class="cta-row">
                <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/en/docs/installation">Installation guide <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
                <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/en/docs/first-steps">First configuration</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
